{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "ULQ2003AQDRQ1",
 "kind": "bjt",
 "manufacturer": "Texas Instruments",
 "title": "ULQ2003A-Q1 and ULQ2004A-Q1: seven-channel 50 V, 500 mA NPN Darlington arrays for automotive use",
 "source": {
  "document": "SGLS148F",
  "revision": "December 2002, revised June 2024",
  "pages": 30
 },
 "summary": "Seven NPN Darlington sinks in one 16-pin package, each with an open collector rated 50 V and 500 mA, all emitters joined at pin E, and a clamp diode from every collector to a shared COM pin for inductive loads. A series base resistor sits in every input: 2.7 kΩ in the ULQ2003A-Q1 for TTL and 5 V CMOS drive, 10.5 kΩ in the ULQ2004A-Q1 for CMOS on 6 V to 15 V supplies. Outputs may be paralleled for more current. ULQ2003AQDRQ1 is the ULQ2003A-Q1 in SOIC-16 (D) rated -40 °C to 125 °C, on a 2500-piece reel.",
