  {
   "id": "inductive-load",
   "title": "ULQ2003A-Q1 as an inductive load driver",
   "page": 13,
   "description": "Three 3.3 V logic outputs drive the seven channels in groups: one drives inputs 1 and 2, one drives 3 and 4, one drives 5, 6 and 7. The matching outputs are tied together so each coil is sunk by two or three paralleled channels. Each coil, drawn as its inductance in series with its resistance, runs from VSUP to its output group. COM goes to VSUP so the clamp diodes catch the coil current at turn-off; E is ground.",
